Problem 15 — Find Pivot Index

Topic: Arrays + Prefix Sum
Difficulty: Easy → Medium
LeetCode: LeetCode 724 — Find Pivot Index

Problem

Given an integer array nums, find the pivot index.

The pivot index is the index where:

sum of elements to the LEFT
=
sum of elements to the RIGHT

The pivot element itself is not included in either sum.

If there are multiple pivot indices, return the leftmost one.

If no pivot index exists, return -1.

Example
Input:
nums = [1,7,3,6,5,6]

Output:
3

Because at index 3:

Left:  1 + 7 + 3 = 11
Right: 5 + 6     = 11
Constraints
1 <= nums.length <= 10^4
-1000 <= nums[i] <= 1000
Test Cases
console.log("===== Problem 15: Find Pivot Index =====");

// 1
console.log("1", pivotIndex([1,7,3,6,5,6]));
// Expected: 3

// 2
console.log("2", pivotIndex([1,2,3]));
// Expected: -1

// 3
console.log("3", pivotIndex([2,1,-1]));
// Expected: 0

// 4
console.log("4", pivotIndex([1,2,1]));
// Expected: 1

// 5
console.log("5", pivotIndex([0,0,0,0]));
// Expected: 0

// 6
console.log("6", pivotIndex([1,-1,0]));
// Expected: 2

// 7
console.log("7", pivotIndex([0,1,-1]));
// Expected: 0

// 8
console.log("8", pivotIndex([-1,-1,-1,0,1,1]));
// Expected: 0

// 9
console.log("9", pivotIndex([1,1,1,1,1]));
// Expected: 2

// 10
console.log("10", pivotIndex([5]));
// Expected: 0

// 11
console.log("11", pivotIndex([-1]));
// Expected: 0

// 12
console.log("12", pivotIndex([10,0,0,0,0]));
// Expected: 0

// 13
console.log("13", pivotIndex([0,0,0,1]));
// Expected: 0

// 14
console.log("14", pivotIndex([1,2,0,3]));
// Expected: 2

// 15
console.log("15", pivotIndex([-2,5,1,2,3,4,-2]));
// Expected: 2

// 16
console.log("16", pivotIndex([2,3,-1,8,4]));
// Expected: 3

// 17
console.log("17", pivotIndex([1,-1,1,-1,1,-1]));
// Expected: 0

// 18
console.log("18", pivotIndex([100,-100,0]));
// Expected: 2

// 19
console.log("19", pivotIndex([3,3,3,3]));
// Expected: -1

// 20
console.log("20", pivotIndex([0]));
// Expected: 0
What I want from you

Try to achieve:

Time:  O(n)
Space: O(1)

Hint: You don't need to calculate the left and right sums repeatedly. Think about calculating the total sum first.
